    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72740.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Probably not, because we didn't have attempts to actually look at what the problems were. We got distracted by this whole work requirement thing, which is, you know, You know, this is pushed by this right-wing outfit in Florida that's a bunch of former staffers that pay themselves $200,000 to $300,000 a year to go around and sell this. It sounds good on the surface. You know, we're going to make people work. You know, if they're going to get help from the government, the problem is there was no, there was nothing in there that was actually going to help people get to work. All that was in there was a requirement that if you're 50 to 60 years old and get laid off, you're going to have to go sit there old 20 hours a week in front of a computer and send out resumes and make phone calls. There's no help in terms of recraining or anything like that because the money was not available to do what needed to be done. So the Senate wasn't going to do it. No, the House Democrats weren't going to do it. Now we'll see what the secretary does. Uh, hopefully they'll do the right things, but you know, we abdicated our chance to do it.",
