    "turn_text": "Not really, um, you know, having gone through this before and with a different president, obviously, but You know, the people that lose out in the legislative process, those same people who ran into the department and lobby the department during the implementation. And a lot of times they're successful there when they vote successful with us. And sometimes they can change the whole meaning of what you were trying to do. They did that to us on some of the provisions in the OA bills. So I think the secretary, current secretary, has paid attention. to what we're doing and why we're doing it. And I don't, at this point, have any indication that he's not going to do anything that doesn't follow legislative intent. But given what happened last time, I pay attention. And we should. part of our job",
