    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Well, he's a secretary and it's, you know, he's got the ability to make certain changes with any of his power. I personally am not convinced that this is something that needs to be done. He's apparently bought a lot of people off because he's all kinds of people running around thinking they're going to move these agencies to their town or their state or whatever. And so they are going along with it. I'm one that's not really I think I'm on the side of the people that are in those agencies who do not want to move and who do not think it's a good idea. I just haven't been, nobody's convinced me that this is why we're doing this or why. You know, this is going to be a great thing. But, you know, he has the ability to do it. And I think maybe the Congress is going to go along with it. So we'll see.",
